---
description: Backend and API rules for server-side code and data layers
version: 1.5.0
globs: [
  "backend/**",
  "server/**",
  "api/**",
  "functions/**",
  "services/**",
  "src/server/**",
  "src/api/**",
  "src/functions/**",
  "**/*.py",
  "**/*.go",
  "**/*.rb",
  "**/*.java",
  "**/*.kt"
]
alwaysApply: false
---

- Keep API contracts documented; update schemas and examples with breaking or visible changes.
- Validate all external inputs at boundaries; return typed errors with safe messages.
- Enforce authZ-aware rate limits/quotas and abuse protection (bot/DoS) on public endpoints.
- Make operations idempotent where feasible; include retries with backoff for outbound calls.
- Set explicit timeouts on network and database calls; avoid unbounded waits.
- Add metrics/tracing for key paths; log failures with correlation identifiers, not secrets.
- Apply migrations forward-only; ship backward-compatible schema changes when possible.
- Guard long-running jobs with cancellation, progress logging, and alerting on failures.
- Wrap data access in transactions when multiple writes must stay consistent.
- Cover critical paths with tests (happy path, error path, and boundary conditions).
